messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S01
Scenario title: Verification Test Setup and Reporting
Initial workflow description:
An engineer prepares a verification test, runs the evaluation, checks the results, and writes a short report. If something looks wrong, the engineer investigates and shares the result with related people.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or condition starts the verification test workflow — for example, is it triggered by a fixed schedule, a request from another team, or a decision made by the engineer?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "What are the distinct steps the engineer performs when preparing the verification test, and are any of those steps performed in an external tool or system?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "What specific criteria or thresholds does the engineer use to decide that a result 'looks wrong' and requires investigation?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "When an investigation is triggered, what steps does it involve, and can it result in re-running the test or does it always end with sharing findings?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Who are the 'related people' that receive the shared result, and through what channel is that result communicated to them?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What information must the short report contain, and where is it submitted or stored once it is written?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Run a verification test and distribute a summarized result report.",
  "actors": [
    "verification engineer",
    "review engineer",
    "project owner"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "test execution tool",
    "result repository",
    "report template",
    "email or collaboration tool"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "test request",
    "test condition",
    "sample identifier",
    "evaluation setup guide"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "test result files",
    "summary report",
    "issue list",
    "review notification"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Review test request and conditions",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Prepare evaluation setup",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Run verification test",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Collect result files",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Check result validity",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Summarize findings in report",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Share report for review",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Review report and request clarification if needed",
      "actor": "review engineer"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are the result files complete and readable?",
      "branches": [
        "complete",
        "missing or corrupted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Do the results contain abnormal patterns?",
      "branches": [
        "normal",
        "abnormal"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing setup information",
    "test execution failure",
    "incomplete result files",
    "unclear abnormal pattern"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Result file collection is repetitive and follows a standard folder or repository pattern."
    },
    {
      "target": "A5",
      "rationale": "Completeness and basic validity checks can be rule-based."
    },
    {
      "target": "A6",
      "rationale": "Report drafting can be supported by template filling and result summarization."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: this expert answers vaguely and never commits to specifics.
Do not name any actor, system, artifact, threshold, condition or exception from the reference workflow.
Use hedged generalities such as "the person in charge usually checks it before it goes out".
Answer every question in this style, at most 30 words each.

